1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:00,953
Exhibit A.

2
00:00:01,003 --> 00:00:02,913
A number in a dashboard moved.

3
00:00:02,963 --> 00:00:08,204
Exhibit A puts every explanation on trial and returns a verdict with evidence for

4
00:00:08,254 --> 00:00:08,988
every claim.

5
00:00:09,717 --> 00:00:14,813
In October 2020, 15,841 positive tests went missing from England's COVID dashboard

6
00:00:14,863 --> 00:00:17,888
because a case file hit a spreadsheet size limit.

7
00:00:17,938 --> 00:00:19,332
The patients were told;

8
00:00:19,382 --> 00:00:23,223
an estimated 50,000 of their close contacts were never traced.

9
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:27,428
Analytics teams meet the same failure every week at smaller stakes:

10
00:00:27,478 --> 00:00:32,637
a number moves, and duplication, a missing source, a concept switch and real growth

11
00:00:32,687 --> 00:00:34,269
look identical on a chart.

12
00:00:34,319 --> 00:00:37,219
Is the number real, and which source caused it?

13
00:00:37,269 --> 00:00:39,667
A confident paragraph cannot be re-run.

14
00:00:40,217 --> 00:00:42,132
Exhibit A changes three things.

15
00:00:42,182 --> 00:00:44,097
Every claim becomes an exhibit:

16
00:00:44,147 --> 00:00:47,646
the SQL that ran, its result hash, a one-command re-run.

17
00:00:47,696 --> 00:00:52,083
Every explanation is a hypothesis confirmed or eliminated by evidence.

18
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:55,887
And the verdict is decided by a code gate, never by a model.

19
00:00:56,450 --> 00:00:58,632
Here is the case in the viewer.

20
00:00:58,682 --> 00:01:03,888
The reported Manufacturing series jumps 1.89x, outside the baseline band.

21
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:09,648
The dashed line is the corrected series, one annual fact per company and period.

22
00:01:09,698 --> 00:01:11,592
The jump almost disappears:

23
00:01:11,642 --> 00:01:14,976
$1.29 trillion reported, $49 billion corrected.

24
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,768
The verdict is mixed.

25
00:01:16,818 --> 00:01:20,416
96.2% of the move is a filing-year duplication artifact;

26
00:01:20,466 --> 00:01:21,263
3.8% is real.

27
00:01:21,313 --> 00:01:26,279
The shares come from a counterfactual, and the gate checks that each cause is

28
00:01:26,329 --> 00:01:31,751
located in the lineage, quantified, corroborated by an independent source, and timed

29
00:01:31,801 --> 00:01:32,728
to the symptom.

30
00:01:33,183 --> 00:01:34,721
Five hypotheses go on trial.

31
00:01:34,771 --> 00:01:36,990
The suspects are selected from the data.

32
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:40,280
The filer whose facts all land in the onset year is Apple.

33
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:43,570
The filer whose history stops before the window is Target.

34
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:47,937
The fastest-growing filer in the segment is Tesla, cleared at 4% of the jump.

35
00:01:47,987 --> 00:01:49,525
No company is named in code.

36
00:01:49,983 --> 00:01:52,034
Three Nemotron roles, all bounded.

37
00:01:52,084 --> 00:01:56,976
Embeddings re-score memory recall, so this warm case finds the closed one at 72%

38
00:01:57,026 --> 00:01:57,656
similarity.

39
00:01:57,706 --> 00:02:02,351
The Defense Counsel critic raises five objections and cannot change a share.

40
00:02:02,401 --> 00:02:06,181
The content-safety model labels the finding as a second guard.

41
00:02:06,650 --> 00:02:11,490
When the verdict is an artifact, the repair is proven first on an isolated shadow

42
00:02:11,540 --> 00:02:16,319
view under a signed contract, with 7 invariants and two deliberately bad repairs

43
00:02:16,369 --> 00:02:17,224
that must fail.

44
00:02:17,274 --> 00:02:22,054
Then approval is a separate operator action that signs exactly 7 statements, and

45
00:02:22,104 --> 00:02:25,857
writeback executes only those and re-reads everything it wrote:

46
00:02:25,907 --> 00:02:26,400
8 checks.

47
00:02:26,883 --> 00:02:29,519
This is the recorded live close on Zetaris:

48
00:02:29,569 --> 00:02:34,764
the corrected view, a USL with a composite key and a data-quality rule, zero invalid

49
00:02:34,814 --> 00:02:37,637
records, and the original view hash unchanged.

50
00:02:37,687 --> 00:02:39,697
The full case log is in the repo.

51
00:02:40,650 --> 00:02:42,560
Generality is shown, not claimed.

52
00:02:42,610 --> 00:02:45,412
The same investigator runs on sector net income.

53
00:02:45,462 --> 00:02:47,253
Services looks like it doubled;

54
00:02:47,303 --> 00:02:52,005
the suspect this time is IBM, whose earlier periods were filed under a different

55
00:02:52,055 --> 00:02:54,856
concept, and the corrected series actually fell.

56
00:02:54,906 --> 00:02:55,332
Verdict:

57
00:02:55,382 --> 00:02:56,163
DATA_ARTIFACT.

58
00:02:56,213 --> 00:02:58,480
Nothing in the hypothesis code changed.

59
00:02:59,450 --> 00:03:01,042
Zetaris is the fact path:

60
00:03:01,092 --> 00:03:05,770
federated SQL, inferred lineage, schema-store views and a keyed USL with

61
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:08,726
data-quality rules, behind a read-only guard.

62
00:03:08,776 --> 00:03:13,783
Meterless contracts carry memory, bounded context, lineage and signed intent.

63
00:03:13,833 --> 00:03:16,344
Nemotron critiques, guards and recalls.

64
00:03:16,917 --> 00:03:17,440
69 tests.

65
00:03:17,490 --> 00:03:22,476
20 claim checks across a cold run, a warm run, an ablation and a second metric,

66
00:03:22,526 --> 00:03:25,281
reproducing their result file byte for byte.

67
00:03:25,331 --> 00:03:30,381
A Docker image, a static viewer on GitHub Pages, and the live close committed as

68
00:03:30,431 --> 00:03:30,955
evidence.

69
00:03:31,517 --> 00:03:35,976
Track one asks for a clever ability to discover and work across fragmented data

70
00:03:36,026 --> 00:03:36,433
sources.

71
00:03:36,483 --> 00:03:41,170
Exhibit A infers the sources behind a metric, finds the concept a filer moved to or

72
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:45,908
from, corroborates through a second channel, and writes the fix back where the data

73
00:03:45,958 --> 00:03:46,358
lives.

74
00:03:46,817 --> 00:03:47,624
Exhibit A.

75
00:03:47,674 --> 00:03:50,369
Adjudication, not summarization.

76
00:03:50,419 --> 00:03:55,858
The repo, the evals, the live case and a read-only viewer are at

77
00:03:55,908 --> 00:03:58,431
github.com/big14way/exhibit-a.

